IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulations 21 to 25: internal controls (21), notification to the FCA by an authorised person (23), training (24) and
-- supervisory action against a relevant parent undertaking (25).  Regulation 22 is blank in this text.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- TIME.  "Within N days of X" is read as: the last day is X plus N, and the day X itself is not counted (Marginal readings, (d)).
-- "Within 30 days beginning with the date" is read as: the date itself is the first of the 30 days, so the last day is the date plus 29.
-- The Interpretation Act 1978 is not staged for this text (NOTES, Dependencies); a period that Act would count differently (a day on which
-- the office is closed) is not handled.  Each timed duty has a decision function over two dates and a regulative rule run with #TRACE.

§ `Regulation 21 -- Internal controls`

-- reg 21(6).  Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply where the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in
-- association with any other person.
-- src:616 | (6) Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply where the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person.
@ref reg 21(6) (src:616-616)
GIVEN `the relevant person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person employs any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person acts in association with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(6) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person is an individual` AND (NOT (`the relevant person employs any other person`)) AND (NOT (`the relevant person acts in association with any other person`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply where the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person" (Ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)

-- reg 21(1).  Where appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business, a relevant person must (a) appoint one individual who is a
-- member of the board of directors (or its equivalent) or of senior management as the officer responsible for compliance with these
-- Regulations; (b) carry out screening of relevant employees before the appointment is made and during it; (c) establish an independent
-- audit function with the responsibility (i) to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of the policies, controls and
-- procedures, (ii) to make recommendations, and (iii) to monitor compliance with those recommendations.
-- src:594 | (1) Where appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business, a relevant person must—
-- src:595 | (a) appoint one individual who is a member of the board of directors (or if there is no board, of its equivalent management body) or of its senior management as the officer responsible for the relevant person's compliance with these Regulations;
-- src:596 | (b) carry out screening of relevant employees appointed by the relevant person, both before the appointment is made and during the course of the appointment;
-- src:597 | (c) establish an independent audit function with the responsibility—
-- src:598 | (i) to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of the policies, controls and procedures adopted by the relevant person to comply with the requirements of these Regulations;
-- src:599 | (ii) to make recommendations in relation to those policies, controls and procedures; and
-- src:600 | (iii) to monitor the relevant person's compliance with those recommendations.
@ref reg 21(1) (src:594-600)
GIVEN `it has appointed one individual who is a member of the board of directors (or if there is no board, of its equivalent management body) or of its senior management as the officer responsible for the relevant person's compliance with these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it before the appointment is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it during the course of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has established an independent audit function with the responsibility to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the independent audit function has the responsibility to make recommendations in relation to those policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the independent audit function has the responsibility to monitor the relevant person's compliance with those recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (1): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "it is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (1): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (1): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person"
        IF `it has appointed one individual who is a member of the board of directors (or if there is no board, of its equivalent management body) or of its senior management as the officer responsible for the relevant person's compliance with these Regulations` AND `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it before the appointment is made` AND `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it during the course of the appointment` AND `it has established an independent audit function with the responsibility to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures` AND `the independent audit function has the responsibility to make recommendations in relation to those policies, controls and procedures` AND `the independent audit function has the responsibility to monitor the relevant person's compliance with those recommendations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 21(2)(a).  For paragraph (1)(b), "screening" means an assessment of (i) the skills, knowledge and expertise of the individual to carry
-- out their functions effectively, and (ii) the conduct and integrity of the individual.
-- src:601 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b)—
-- src:602 | (a) “screening” means an assessment of—
-- src:603 | (i) the skills, knowledge and expertise of the individual to carry out their functions effectively;
-- src:604 | (ii) the conduct and integrity of the individual;
@ref reg 21(2)(a) (src:601-604)
GIVEN `it assesses the skills, knowledge and expertise of the individual to carry out their functions effectively` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it assesses the conduct and integrity of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(2)(a) the assessment is screening` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it assesses the skills, knowledge and expertise of the individual to carry out their functions effectively` AND `it assesses the conduct and integrity of the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“screening” means an assessment of— (i) the skills, knowledge and expertise of the individual ...; (ii) the conduct and integrity of the individual"

-- reg 21(2)(b).  A relevant employee is an employee whose work is (i) relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in
-- these Regulations, or (ii) otherwise capable of contributing to the (aa) identification or mitigation of the risks of money laundering,
-- terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the business is subject, or (bb) prevention or detection of money laundering,
-- terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the business.
-- src:605 | (b) a relevant employee is an employee whose work is—
-- src:606 | (i) relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in these Regulations, or
-- src:607 | (ii) otherwise capable of contributing to the—
-- src:608 | (aa) identification or mitigation of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the relevant person's business is subject, or
-- src:609 | (bb) prevention or detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the relevant person's business.
@ref reg 21(2)(b) (src:605-609)
GIVEN `the person is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the identification or mitigation of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the relevant person's business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the prevention or detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the relevant person's business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(2)(b) the employee is a relevant employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an employee` AND (`the work is relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in these Regulations` OR `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the identification or mitigation of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the relevant person's business is subject` OR `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the prevention or detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the relevant person's business`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant employee is an employee whose work is— (i) relevant to the relevant person's compliance ..., or (ii) otherwise capable of contributing to the ..."

-- reg 21(3).  An individual in the relevant person's firm must be appointed as a nominated officer.
-- src:610 | (3) An individual in the relevant person's firm must be appointed as a nominated officer.
@ref reg 21(3) (src:610-610)
GIVEN `an individual in the relevant person's firm has been appointed as a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (3): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(3) the relevant person has appointed a nominated officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (3): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (3): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person"
        IF `an individual in the relevant person's firm has been appointed as a nominated officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual in the relevant person's firm must be appointed as a nominated officer" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 21(4).  A relevant person must, within 14 days of the appointment, inform its supervisory authority of (a) the identity of the individual
-- first appointed under paragraph (1)(a); (b) the identity of the individual first appointed under paragraph (3); and (c) of any subsequent
-- appointment to either of those positions.
-- src:611 | (4) A relevant person must, within 14 days of the appointment, inform its supervisory authority of—
-- src:612 | (a) the identity of the individual first appointed under paragraph (1)(a);
-- src:613 | (b) the identity of the individual first appointed under paragraph (3); and
-- src:614 | (c) of any subsequent appointment to either of those positions.
@ref reg 21(4) (src:611-614)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 21(4) the period of 14 days` MEANS 14

@ref reg 21(4) (src:611-614)
GIVEN `the date of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the relevant person informed its supervisory authority` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(4) the relevant person informed its supervisory authority within 14 days of the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the relevant person informed its supervisory authority`) MINUS (Day `the date of the appointment`) LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days of the appointment" speaks of the days after the appointment (Ruling 2026-11-05, (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words; a date before the period begins is outside it, fork F-period)
        IF (Day `the date on which the relevant person informed its supervisory authority`) MINUS (Day `the date of the appointment`) AT MOST `reg 21(4) the period of 14 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days of the appointment, inform its supervisory authority" (Marginal readings, (c) and (d): a requirement not done is read as the text's no; the day of the appointment is not counted)

DECLARE `reg 21(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 21(4) the relevant person`

DECLARE `reg 21(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 21(4) inform the supervisory authority of the appointment`

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  Time zero is the day of the appointment; the deadline is inclusive (an act at 14 is in time).
`reg 21(4) the duty to inform the supervisory authority within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 21(4) the relevant person`
    MUST `reg 21(4) inform the supervisory authority of the appointment`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 21(4) the relevant person` BECAUSE "the supervisory authority was not informed within 14 days of the appointment"

#TRACE `reg 21(4) the duty to inform the supervisory authority within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 21(4) the relevant person` DOES `reg 21(4) inform the supervisory authority of the appointment` AT 14

#TRACE `reg 21(4) the duty to inform the supervisory authority within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- reg 21(5).  Where a disclosure is made to the nominated officer, that officer must consider it in the light of any relevant information
-- available to the relevant person and determine whether it gives rise to knowledge or suspicion or reasonable grounds for knowledge or
-- suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing.
-- src:615 | (5) Where a disclosure is made to the nominated officer, that officer must consider it in the light of any relevant information which is available to the relevant person and determine whether it gives rise to knowledge or suspicion or reasonable grounds for knowledge or suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref reg 21(5) (src:615-615)
GIVEN `the nominated officer has considered the disclosure in the light of any relevant information which is available to the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominated officer has determined whether the disclosure gives rise to knowledge or suspicion or reasonable grounds for knowledge or suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disclosure has been made to the nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5) the nominated officer has considered the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a disclosure has been made to the nominated officer`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "a disclosure has been made to the nominated officer" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the nominated officer has considered the disclosure in the light of any relevant information which is available to the relevant person` AND `the nominated officer has determined whether the disclosure gives rise to knowledge or suspicion or reasonable grounds for knowledge or suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that officer must consider it in the light of any relevant information which is available to the relevant person and determine whether it gives rise to knowledge or suspicion" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 21(7).  A relevant person who is an electronic money issuer or a payment service provider must appoint an individual to monitor and
-- manage compliance with, and the internal communication of, the policies, controls and procedures adopted under regulation 19(1) or 19A(1),
-- and in particular to (a) identify any situations of higher risk; (b) maintain a record of its policies, controls and procedures, risk
-- assessment and risk management; (c) apply measures to ensure that its policies are taken into account in all relevant functions; and (d)
-- provide information to senior management about their operation and effectiveness whenever appropriate and at least annually.
-- src:617 | (7) A relevant person who is an electronic money issuer or a payment service provider must appoint an individual to monitor and manage compliance with, and the internal communication of, the policies, controls and procedures adopted by the relevant person under regulation 19(1) or 19A(1), and in particular to—
-- src:618 | (a) identify any situations of higher risk of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing;
-- src:619 | (b) maintain a record of its policies, controls and procedures, risk assessment and risk management including the application of such policies and procedures;
-- src:620 | (c) apply measures to ensure that its policies, controls and procedures are taken into account in all relevant functions including in the development of new products, dealing with new customers and in changes to business activities; and
-- src:621 | (d) provide information to senior management about the operation and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures whenever appropriate and at least annually.
@ref reg 21(7) (src:617-621)
GIVEN `it has appointed an individual to monitor and manage compliance with, and the internal communication of, the policies, controls and procedures adopted under regulation 19(1) or 19A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual identifies any situations of higher risk of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual maintains a record of its policies, controls and procedures, risk assessment and risk management including the application of such policies and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual applies measures to ensure that its policies, controls and procedures are taken into account in all relevant functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual provides information to senior management about the operation and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures whenever appropriate and at least annually` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is an electronic money issuer or a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(7) the electronic money issuer or payment service provider has appointed the individual paragraph (7) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is an electronic money issuer or a payment service provider`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant person is an electronic money issuer or a payment service provider" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF `it has appointed an individual to monitor and manage compliance with, and the internal communication of, the policies, controls and procedures adopted under regulation 19(1) or 19A(1)` AND `the individual identifies any situations of higher risk of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` AND `the individual maintains a record of its policies, controls and procedures, risk assessment and risk management including the application of such policies and procedures` AND `the individual applies measures to ensure that its policies, controls and procedures are taken into account in all relevant functions` AND `the individual provides information to senior management about the operation and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures whenever appropriate and at least annually` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person who is an electronic money issuer or a payment service provider must appoint an individual to monitor and manage compliance" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 21(8).  A relevant person must establish and maintain systems which enable it to respond fully and rapidly to enquiries from any
-- person specified in paragraph (9) as to (a) whether it maintains, or has maintained during the previous five years, a business
-- relationship with any person; and (b) the nature of that relationship.
-- src:622 | (8) A relevant person must establish and maintain systems which enable it to respond fully and rapidly to enquiries from any person specified in paragraph (9) as to—
-- src:623 | (a) whether it maintains, or has maintained during the previous five years, a business relationship with any person; and
-- src:624 | (b) the nature of that relationship.
@ref reg 21(8) (src:622-624)
GIVEN `it has established systems which enable it to respond fully and rapidly to enquiries from a person specified in paragraph (9) as to whether it maintains, or has maintained during the previous five years, a business relationship with any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those systems enable it to respond fully and rapidly to such enquiries as to the nature of that relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains those systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(8) the relevant person has established and maintains the systems paragraph (8) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has established systems which enable it to respond fully and rapidly to enquiries from a person specified in paragraph (9) as to whether it maintains, or has maintained during the previous five years, a business relationship with any person` AND `those systems enable it to respond fully and rapidly to such enquiries as to the nature of that relationship` AND `it maintains those systems` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must establish and maintain systems which enable it to respond fully and rapidly to enquiries" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 21(8)(a), the previous five years.  A business relationship "has been maintained during the previous five years" if its last day falls
-- on or after the day five years before the enquiry (Marginal readings, (d)).
@ref reg 21(8) (src:622-624)
GIVEN `the last date on which the business relationship was maintained` IS A DATE
      `the date of the enquiry` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(8)(a) the business relationship was maintained during the previous five years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the last date on which the business relationship was maintained`) AT LEAST (Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the date of the enquiry`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of the enquiry`) ((DATE_YEAR `the date of the enquiry`) MINUS 5))) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "maintains, or has maintained during the previous five years, a business relationship" (the relationship ended before the previous five years)

-- reg 21(9).  The persons specified in this paragraph.
DECLARE `reg 21(9) person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 21(9)(a) a financial investigator accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
    `reg 21(9)(b) a person acting on behalf of the Scottish Ministers in their capacity as an enforcement authority under that Act`
    `reg 21(9)(c) a constable or equivalent officer of any law enforcement authority`
    `reg 21(9) another person`

-- src:625 | (9) The persons specified in this paragraph are—
-- src:626 | (a) financial investigators accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (accreditation and training) ;
-- src:627 | (b) persons acting on behalf of the Scottish Ministers in their capacity as an enforcement authority under that Act; and
-- src:628 | (c) constables or equivalent officers of any law enforcement authority.
@ref reg 21(9) (src:625-628)
GIVEN person IS A `reg 21(9) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(9) the person is specified in this paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `reg 21(9)(a) a financial investigator accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(9)(b) a person acting on behalf of the Scottish Ministers in their capacity as an enforcement authority under that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(9)(c) a constable or equivalent officer of any law enforcement authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(9) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The persons specified in this paragraph are— (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 21(10).  In determining what is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business, a relevant person (a) must take into
-- account its risk assessment under regulation 18(1) and 18A(1); and (b) may take into account any guidance issued by the FCA, or issued by
-- any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
-- src:629 | (10) In determining what is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business, a relevant person—
-- src:630 | (a) must take into account its risk assessment under regulation 18(1) and 18A(1); and
-- src:631 | (b) may take into account any guidance which has been—
-- src:632 | (i) issued by the FCA; or
-- src:633 | (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
@ref reg 21(10) (src:629-633)
GIVEN `it has taken into account its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(10)(a) the relevant person has taken into account its risk assessments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken into account its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` AND `it has taken into account its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person— (a) must take into account its risk assessment under regulation 18(1) and 18A(1)" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

@ref reg 21(10)(b) (src:631-633)
GIVEN `the guidance has been issued by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance has been issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance has been approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 21(10)(b) the relevant person may take the guidance into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance has been issued by the FCA` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the guidance has been issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` AND `the guidance has been approved by the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a relevant person "may take into account any guidance which has been— (i) issued by the FCA; or (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury"

§ `Regulation 23 -- Requirement on authorised person to inform the FCA`

-- reg 23(1).  An authorised person whose supervisory authority is the FCA must, before acting as a money service business or a trust or
-- company service provider or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act as such.
-- src:637 | (1) An authorised person whose supervisory authority is the FCA must, before acting as a money service business or a trust or company service provider or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act as such.
@ref reg 23(1) (src:637-637)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 23(1) the period of 28 days` MEANS 28

@ref reg 23(1) (src:637-637)
GIVEN `the date on which the authorised person began to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 23(1) the authorised person informed the FCA in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the authorised person began to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider`) AT MOST `reg 23(1) the period of 28 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before acting ... or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA" (Marginal readings, (c) and (d): a requirement not done is read as the text's no; the day it began to act is not counted)

DECLARE `reg 23 party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 23 the authorised person`

DECLARE `reg 23 act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 23(1) inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act`
    `reg 23(3) inform the FCA that it has ceased to act`
    `reg 23(3A) provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy`

-- Time zero is the day the person began to act.  Informing the FCA before that day is in time, so only the later deadline is traced.
`reg 23(1) the duty to inform the FCA within 28 days of beginning to act` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 23 the authorised person`
    MUST `reg 23(1) inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 23 the authorised person` BECAUSE "the FCA was not informed before acting or within 28 days of beginning to act"

#TRACE `reg 23(1) the duty to inform the FCA within 28 days of beginning to act` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 23 the authorised person` DOES `reg 23(1) inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act` AT 28

#TRACE `reg 23(1) the duty to inform the FCA within 28 days of beginning to act` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)

-- reg 23(2).  Paragraph (1) does not apply to an authorised person which (a) immediately before the day on which these Regulations come
-- into force ("the relevant date") was acting as a money service business or a trust or company service provider and continues to act as
-- such after that date; and (b) informs the FCA that it is acting as such within 30 days of the relevant date.
-- src:638 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to an authorised person which—
-- src:639 | (a) immediately before the day on which these Regulations come into force (“the relevant date”) was acting as a money service business or a trust or company service provider and continues to act as such after that date; and
-- src:640 | (b) informs the FCA that it is acting as such within 30 days of the relevant date.
@ref reg 23(2) (src:638-640)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 23(2)(b) the period of 30 days` MEANS 30

@ref reg 23(2) (src:638-640)
GIVEN `the authorised person was acting as a money service business or a trust or company service provider immediately before the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it continues to act as such after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it informed the FCA that it is acting as such` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 23(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the authorised person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authorised person was acting as a money service business or a trust or company service provider immediately before the relevant date` AND `it continues to act as such after that date` AND (Day `the date on which it informed the FCA that it is acting as such`) MINUS (Day `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`) AT MOST `reg 23(2)(b) the period of 30 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply to an authorised person which (a) ...; and (b) informs the FCA ... within 30 days of the relevant date"; the paragraph says nothing of a person outside it (Ruling 2026-11-05, (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words)

-- reg 23(3).  Where an authorised person whose supervisory authority is the FCA ceases to act as a money service business or a trust or
-- company service provider, it must within 28 days inform the FCA.
-- src:641 | (3) Where an authorised person whose supervisory authority is the FCA ceases to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider, it must within 28 days inform the FCA.
@ref reg 23(3) (src:641-641)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 23(3) the period of 28 days` MEANS 28

@ref reg 23(3) (src:641-641)
GIVEN `the date on which the authorised person ceased to act` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 23(3) the authorised person informed the FCA of ceasing to act within 28 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the authorised person ceased to act`) LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 28 days" of ceasing speaks of the days after it ceased (Ruling 2026-11-05, (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words; a date before the period begins is outside it, fork F-period)
        IF (Day `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the authorised person ceased to act`) AT MOST `reg 23(3) the period of 28 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within 28 days inform the FCA" (Marginal readings, (c) and (d))

`reg 23(3) the duty to inform the FCA within 28 days of ceasing to act` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 23 the authorised person`
    MUST `reg 23(3) inform the FCA that it has ceased to act`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 23 the authorised person` BECAUSE "the FCA was not informed within 28 days of ceasing to act"

#TRACE `reg 23(3) the duty to inform the FCA within 28 days of ceasing to act` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 23 the authorised person` DOES `reg 23(3) inform the FCA that it has ceased to act` AT 28

#TRACE `reg 23(3) the duty to inform the FCA within 28 days of ceasing to act` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)

-- reg 23(3A).  If, after an authorised person ("A") has provided the FCA with any information under this regulation, (a) there is a material
-- change affecting any matter contained in that information; or (b) it becomes apparent to A that the information contains an inaccuracy,
-- then A must provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy within 30 days beginning with the date of the
-- occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy.
-- "Thirty days beginning with the date" counts the date itself as the first day, so the thirtieth day is the date plus 29 (Marginal readings, (d)).
-- src:642 | (3A) If, at any time after an authorised person whose supervisory authority is the FCA (“A”) has provided the FCA with any information under this regulation—
-- src:643 | (a) there is a material change affecting any matter contained in that information; or
-- src:644 | (b) it becomes apparent to A that the information contains an inaccuracy,
-- src:645 | then A must provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy within 30 days beginning with the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy.
@ref reg 23(3A) (src:642-645)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 23(3A) the period of 30 days beginning with the date` MEANS 30

@ref reg 23(3A) (src:642-645)
GIVEN `the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE
      `the date on which A provided the FCA with the details or correction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 23(3A) A provided the FCA with the details or correction within 30 days beginning with the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which A provided the FCA with the details or correction`) MINUS (Day `the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy`) LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the period begins "with the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy" (Ruling 2026-11-05, (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words; a date before the period begins is outside it, fork F-period)
        IF (Day `the date on which A provided the FCA with the details or correction`) MINUS (Day `the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy`) AT MOST (`reg 23(3A) the period of 30 days beginning with the date` MINUS 1) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A must provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy within 30 days beginning with the date" (Marginal readings, (c) and (d): the date itself is the first of the 30 days)

`reg 23(3A) the duty to provide the FCA with details or a correction within 30 days beginning with the date` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 23 the authorised person`
    MUST `reg 23(3A) provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy`
    WITHIN 29
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 23 the authorised person` BECAUSE "the FCA was not given details of the change or a correction within 30 days beginning with the date of the change or discovery"

#TRACE `reg 23(3A) the duty to provide the FCA with details or a correction within 30 days beginning with the date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 23 the authorised person` DOES `reg 23(3A) provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy` AT 29

#TRACE `reg 23(3A) the duty to provide the FCA with details or a correction within 30 days beginning with the date` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- reg 23(4).  Any requirement imposed by this regulation is to be treated as if it were a requirement imposed by or under FSMA.
-- src:646 | (4) Any requirement imposed by this regulation is to be treated as if it were a requirement imposed by or under FSMA.
@ref reg 23(4) (src:646-646)
GIVEN `the requirement is imposed by regulation 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 23(4) the requirement is to be treated as a requirement imposed by or under FSMA` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement is imposed by regulation 23` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any requirement imposed by this regulation"; the paragraph says nothing of a requirement imposed elsewhere

-- reg 23(5).  Any information to be provided to the FCA under this regulation must be in such form or verified in such manner as it may specify.
-- src:647 | (5) Any information to be provided to the FCA under this regulation must be in such form or verified in such manner as it may specify.
@ref reg 23(5) (src:647-647)
GIVEN `the information is in the form the FCA has specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is verified in the manner the FCA has specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is to be provided to the FCA under regulation 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 23(5) the information provided to the FCA is in the form and verified in the manner the FCA specifies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the information is to be provided to the FCA under regulation 23`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the information is to be provided to the FCA under regulation 23" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF `the information is in the form the FCA has specified` AND `the information is verified in the manner the FCA has specified` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form or verified in such manner as it may specify" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- SEAM S-9 (answering): regulation 54 asks whether the person has notified the FCA that it is acting, or intends to act, as a money
-- service business or a trust or company service provider.  A fact; this wrapper gives the merge a function to call.
-- src:637 | (1) An authorised person whose supervisory authority is the FCA must, before acting as a money service business or a trust or company service provider or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act as such.
@ref reg 23 (src:637-637)
GIVEN `the person has informed the FCA that it is acting, or intends to act, as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23 the person has notified the FCA that it is acting, or intends to act, as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` MEANS
    `the person has informed the FCA that it is acting, or intends to act, as a money service business or a trust or company service provider`

§ `Regulation 24 -- Training`

-- reg 24(1).  A relevant person must (a) take appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work
-- is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are (i) made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation
-- financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations; and (ii) regularly
-- given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering,
-- terrorist financing or proliferation financing; (b) maintain a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in
-- particular, of the training given.
-- src:649 | (1) A relevant person must—
-- src:650 | (a) take appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees , and any agents it uses for the purposes of its business whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are—
-- src:651 | (i) made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations; and
-- src:652 | (ii) regularly given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing;
-- src:653 | (b) maintain a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in particular, of the training given to its relevant employees and to any agents it uses for the purposes of its business whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2).
@ref reg 24(1) (src:649-653)
GIVEN `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are regularly given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in particular of the training given to its relevant employees and to any such agents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 24(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations` AND `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are regularly given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` AND `it maintains a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in particular of the training given to its relevant employees and to any such agents` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 24(2).  For the purposes of paragraph (1), a relevant employee is an employee whose work is (a) relevant to the relevant person's
-- compliance with any requirement in these Regulations, or (b) otherwise capable of contributing to the (i) identification or mitigation of
-- the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the business is subject; or (ii) prevention or
-- detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the business.
-- src:654 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1), a relevant employee is an employee whose work is—
-- src:655 | (a) relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in these Regulations, or
-- src:656 | (b) otherwise capable of contributing to the—
-- src:657 | (i) identification or mitigation of the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the relevant person's business is subject; or
-- src:658 | (ii) prevention or detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the relevant person's business.
@ref reg 24(2) (src:654-658)
GIVEN `the person is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the identification or mitigation of the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the relevant person's business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the prevention or detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the relevant person's business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 24(2) the employee is a relevant employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an employee` AND (`the work is relevant to the relevant person's compliance with any requirement in these Regulations` OR `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the identification or mitigation of the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which the relevant person's business is subject` OR `the work is otherwise capable of contributing to the prevention or detection of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing in relation to the relevant person's business`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant employee is an employee whose work is— (a) relevant to the relevant person's compliance ..., or (b) otherwise capable of contributing to the ..."

-- reg 24(3).  In determining what measures are appropriate under paragraph (1), a relevant person (a) must take account of (i) the nature of
-- its business; (ii) its size; (iii) the nature and extent of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation
-- financing to which its business is subject; and (b) may take into account any guidance issued by the FCA, or issued by any other
-- supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
-- src:659 | (3) In determining what measures are appropriate under paragraph (1), a relevant person—
-- src:660 | (a) must take account of—
-- src:661 | (i) the nature of its business;
-- src:662 | (ii) its size;
-- src:663 | (iii) the nature and extent of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which its business is subject; and
-- src:664 | (b) may take into account any guidance which has been—
-- src:665 | (i) issued by the FCA; or
-- src:666 | (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
@ref reg 24(3) (src:659-666)
GIVEN `it has taken account of the nature of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of its size` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken account of the nature and extent of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which its business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 24(3)(a) the relevant person has taken account of what sub-paragraph (a) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken account of the nature of its business` AND `it has taken account of its size` AND `it has taken account of the nature and extent of the risks of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing to which its business is subject` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person— (a) must take account of—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

@ref reg 24(3)(b) (src:664-666)
GIVEN `the guidance has been issued by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance has been issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance has been approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 24(3)(b) the relevant person may take the guidance into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance has been issued by the FCA` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the guidance has been issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` AND `the guidance has been approved by the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a relevant person "may take into account any guidance which has been— (i) issued by the FCA; or (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury"

§ `Regulation 25 -- Supervisory action`

-- reg 25(1).  The supervisory authority must determine whether the additional measures taken under regulation 20(4) by a relevant parent
-- undertaking which is an authorised person, a qualifying parent undertaking (section 192B of FSMA) or a non-authorised parent undertaking
-- (section 143B of FSMA) are sufficient to handle the risk of money laundering and terrorist financing effectively.
-- src:668 | (1) The supervisory authority must determine whether the additional measures taken under regulation 20(4) by a relevant parent undertaking which is an authorised person , a qualifying parent undertaking (as defined by section 192B of FSMA) or a non-authorised parent undertaking (as defined by section 143B of FSMA) are sufficient to handle the risk of money laundering and terrorist financing effectively.
@ref reg 25(1) (src:668-668)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has determined whether the additional measures are sufficient to handle the risk of money laundering and terrorist financing effectively` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional measures were taken under regulation 20(4) by a relevant parent undertaking which is an authorised person, a qualifying parent undertaking or a non-authorised parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(1) the supervisory authority has determined whether the additional measures are sufficient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the additional measures were taken under regulation 20(4) by a relevant parent undertaking which is an authorised person, a qualifying parent undertaking or a non-authorised parent undertaking`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the additional measures were taken under regulation 20(4) by a relevant parent undertaking which is an authorised person, a qualifying parent undertaking or a non-authorised parent undertaking" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF `the supervisory authority has determined whether the additional measures are sufficient to handle the risk of money laundering and terrorist financing effectively` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The supervisory authority must determine whether the additional measures taken under regulation 20(4) ... are sufficient" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(2).  If the supervisory authority does not consider the measures sufficient, it must consider whether to direct the relevant parent
-- undertaking (a) not to enter into a business relationship with a specified person; (b) not to undertake transactions of a specified
-- description with a specified person; (c) to terminate an existing business relationship with a specified person; (d) to cease any
-- operations in the third country; (e) to ensure that its subsidiary undertaking (i) does not enter into a business relationship with a
-- specified person; (ii) terminates an existing business relationship with a specified person; or (iii) does not undertake transactions of a
-- specified description with a specified person, or ceases any operations in the third country.
-- src:669 | (2) If the supervisory authority does not consider the measures referred to in paragraph (1) to be sufficient, it must consider whether to direct the relevant parent undertaking—
-- src:670 | (a) not to enter into a business relationship with a specified person;
-- src:671 | (b) not to undertake transactions of a specified description with a specified person;
-- src:672 | (c) to terminate an existing business relationship with a specified person;
-- src:673 | (d) to cease any operations in the third country.
-- src:674 | (e) to ensure that its subsidiary undertaking—
-- src:675 | (i) does not enter into a business relationship with a specified person;
-- src:676 | (ii) terminates an existing business relationship with a specified person; or
-- src:677 | (iii) does not undertake transactions of a specified description with a specified person, or ceases any operations in the third country.
@ref reg 25(2) (src:669-677)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has considered whether to direct the relevant parent undertaking as sub-paragraphs (a) to (e) provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority does not consider the measures referred to in paragraph (1) to be sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(2) the supervisory authority has considered whether to give a direction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the supervisory authority does not consider the measures referred to in paragraph (1) to be sufficient`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the supervisory authority does not consider the measures referred to in paragraph (1) to be sufficient" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the supervisory authority has considered whether to direct the relevant parent undertaking as sub-paragraphs (a) to (e) provide` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must consider whether to direct the relevant parent undertaking—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

DECLARE `reg 25(2) direction` IS ONE OF
    `reg 25(2)(a) not to enter into a business relationship with a specified person`
    `reg 25(2)(b) not to undertake transactions of a specified description with a specified person`
    `reg 25(2)(c) to terminate an existing business relationship with a specified person`
    `reg 25(2)(d) to cease any operations in the third country`
    `reg 25(2)(e) to ensure that its subsidiary undertaking does not enter into or terminates a business relationship, or does not undertake transactions, or ceases any operations`
    `reg 25(2) some other direction`

@ref reg 25(2) (src:669-677)
GIVEN direction IS A `reg 25(2) direction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(2) the direction is one that the supervisory authority must consider whether to give` MEANS
    CONSIDER direction
    WHEN `reg 25(2)(a) not to enter into a business relationship with a specified person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 25(2)(b) not to undertake transactions of a specified description with a specified person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 25(2)(c) to terminate an existing business relationship with a specified person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 25(2)(d) to cease any operations in the third country` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 25(2)(e) to ensure that its subsidiary undertaking does not enter into or terminates a business relationship, or does not undertake transactions, or ceases any operations` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 25(2) some other direction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) names five directions and says nothing of any other

-- SEAM S-19 (answering): regulations 93 and 99 ask whether the decision is a direction under regulation 25(2).  A fact; this wrapper gives
-- the merge a function to call.
@ref reg 25(2) (src:669-677)
GIVEN `the decision is a direction given under regulation 25(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(2) the decision is a direction` MEANS `the decision is a direction given under regulation 25(2)`

-- reg 25(4).  A matter to which a notice relates is still open to review if (a) the period during which any person may refer the matter to
-- the appropriate tribunal is still running; (b) the matter has been referred to the appropriate tribunal but has not been dealt with; (c)
-- it has been referred and dealt with but the period during which an appeal may be brought is still running; or (d) such an appeal has been
-- brought but has not been determined.
-- src:682 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (3), a matter to which a notice relates is still open to review if—
-- src:683 | (a) the period during which any person may refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal is still running;
-- src:684 | (b) the matter has been referred to the appropriate tribunal but has not been dealt with;
-- src:685 | (c) the matter has been referred to the appropriate tribunal and dealt with but the period during which an appeal may be brought against the appropriate tribunal's decision is still running; or
-- src:686 | (d) such an appeal has been brought but has not been determined.
@ref reg 25(4) (src:682-686)
GIVEN `the period during which any person may refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal is still running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter has been referred to the appropriate tribunal but has not been dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter has been dealt with but the period during which an appeal may be brought against the decision is still running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such an appeal has been brought but has not been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(4) the matter to which the notice relates is still open to review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the period during which any person may refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal is still running` OR `the matter has been referred to the appropriate tribunal but has not been dealt with` OR `the matter has been dealt with but the period during which an appeal may be brought against the decision is still running` OR `such an appeal has been brought but has not been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a matter to which a notice relates is still open to review if— (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..." (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 25(3)(b).  A direction takes effect on such date as may be specified in the notice.
-- src:678 | (3) A direction issued under paragraph (2) takes effect—
-- src:679 | (a) immediately, if the notice given under paragraph (6) states that that is the case;
-- src:680 | (b) on such date as may be specified in the notice; or
-- src:681 | (c) if no such date is specified in the notice, when the matter to which the notice relates is no longer open to review.
@ref reg 25(3) (src:678-681)
GIVEN `the date specified in the notice on which the direction takes effect` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(3)(b) the date specified in the notice has come` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date specified in the notice on which the direction takes effect`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (Day `the date on which the question is asked`) AT LEAST (Day specified) THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) on such date as may be specified in the notice" (that date has not yet come)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (3)(b) speaks of "such date as may be specified in the notice" and no date is specified

-- reg 25(3).  A direction issued under paragraph (2) takes effect (a) immediately, if the notice given under paragraph (6) states that that is
-- the case; (b) on such date as may be specified in the notice; or (c) if no such date is specified in the notice, when the matter to which the
-- notice relates is no longer open to review.
@ref reg 25(3) (src:678-681)
GIVEN `the notice states that the direction takes effect immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a date is specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 25(3)(b) the date specified in the notice has come` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 25(4) the matter to which the notice relates is still open to review` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(3) the direction has taken effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice states that the direction takes effect immediately` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a date is specified in the notice` THEN `reg 25(3)(b) the date specified in the notice has come`
        IF `reg 25(4) the matter to which the notice relates is still open to review` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 25(4) the matter to which the notice relates is still open to review` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) if no such date is specified in the notice, when the matter to which the notice relates is no longer open to review" (the matter is still open)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the matter is still open to review has not been answered

-- reg 25(5).  Where the FCA proposes to issue a direction under paragraph (2) to a PRA-authorised person or to a person who has a
-- qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person, it must consult the PRA.
-- src:687 | (5) Where the FCA proposes to issue a direction under paragraph (2) to a PRA-authorised person or to a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person, it must consult the PRA.
@ref reg 25(5) (src:687-687)
GIVEN `the FCA has consulted the PRA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA proposes to issue a direction under paragraph (2) to a PRA-authorised person or to a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(5) the FCA has consulted the PRA` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the FCA proposes to issue a direction under paragraph (2) to a PRA-authorised person or to a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the FCA proposes to issue a direction under paragraph (2) to a PRA-authorised person or to a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the FCA has consulted the PRA` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must consult the PRA" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(6).  If the supervisory authority issues a direction under paragraph (2) it must give the relevant parent undertaking ("A") a notice in writing.
