        IF NOT (`the supervisory authority has issued a direction under paragraph (2)`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the supervisory authority has issued a direction under paragraph (2)" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the supervisory authority has given the relevant parent undertaking a notice in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must give the relevant parent undertaking (“A”) a notice in writing" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(7).  The notice must (a) give details of the direction; (b) state the supervisory authority's reasons for issuing it; (c) inform A
-- that A may make representations within such period as may be specified in the notice (whether or not A has referred the matter to the
-- appropriate tribunal); (d) inform A of when the direction takes effect; and (e) inform A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal.
-- src:689 | (7) The notice must—
-- src:690 | (a) give details of the direction;
-- src:691 | (b) state the supervisory authority's reasons for issuing the direction;
-- src:692 | (c) inform A that A may make representations to the supervisory authority within such period as may be specified in the notice (whether or not A has referred the matter to the appropriate tribunal);
-- src:693 | (d) inform A of when the direction takes effect; and
-- src:694 | (e) inform A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal.
@ref reg 25(7) (src:689-694)
GIVEN `the notice gives details of the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the supervisory authority's reasons for issuing the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice informs A that A may make representations to the supervisory authority within such period as may be specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice informs A of when the direction takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice informs A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(7) the notice contains what paragraph (7) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice gives details of the direction` AND `the notice states the supervisory authority's reasons for issuing the direction` AND `the notice informs A that A may make representations to the supervisory authority within such period as may be specified in the notice` AND `the notice informs A of when the direction takes effect` AND `the notice informs A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(8).  The supervisory authority may extend the period allowed under the notice for making representations.
-- src:695 | (8) The supervisory authority may extend the period allowed under the notice for making representations.
@ref reg 25(8) (src:695-695)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority extends the period allowed under the notice for making representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(8) the supervisory authority may extend the period allowed under the notice for making representations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the supervisory authority extends the period allowed under the notice for making representations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (8) says the authority "may extend" the period; it does not say it must

-- reg 25(9).  If, having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority decides (a) to issue the direction, or (b) if the
-- direction has been issued, not to rescind the direction, it must give A notice in writing.
-- src:696 | (9) If, having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority decides—
-- src:697 | (a) to issue the direction, or
-- src:698 | (b) if the direction has been issued, not to rescind the direction,
-- src:699 | it must give A notice in writing.
@ref reg 25(9) (src:696-699)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has given A notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority has decided to issue the direction or, if the direction has been issued, not to rescind it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(9) the supervisory authority has given A notice in writing of its decision to issue or not to rescind` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority has decided to issue the direction or, if the direction has been issued, not to rescind it`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority has decided to issue the direction or, if the direction has been issued, not to rescind it" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the supervisory authority has given A notice in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must give A notice in writing" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(10).  If, having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority decides (a) not to issue the direction, (b) to
-- issue a different direction, or (c) to rescind a direction which has effect, it must give A notice in writing.
-- src:700 | (10) If, having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority decides—
-- src:701 | (a) not to issue the direction,
-- src:702 | (b) to issue a different direction, or
-- src:703 | (c) to rescind a direction which has effect,
-- src:704 | it must give A notice in writing.
