GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(10) the supervisory authority has given A notice in writing of its decision not to issue, to issue a different direction or to rescind` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority has decided not to issue the direction, to issue a different direction, or to rescind a direction which has effect`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "having considered any representations made by A, the supervisory authority has decided not to issue the direction, to issue a different direction, or to rescind a direction which has effect" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the supervisory authority has given A notice in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must give A notice in writing" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(11).  A notice under paragraph (9) must inform A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal.
-- src:705 | (11) A notice under paragraph (9) must inform A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal.
@ref reg 25(11) (src:705-705)
