        IF `the notice informs A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must inform A of A's right to refer the matter to the appropriate tribunal" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(12).  A notice under paragraph (10)(b) must comply with paragraph (7).
