-- reg 25(13A).  The supervisory authority may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish such information about a direction given
-- under paragraph (2) as the authority considers appropriate.
-- src:708 | (13A) The supervisory authority may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish such information about a direction given under paragraph (2) as the authority considers appropriate.
@ref reg 25(13A) (src:708-708)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority considers it proportionate to publish information about the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(13A) the supervisory authority may publish information about the direction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the supervisory authority considers it proportionate to publish information about the direction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish such information" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 25(13B).  Where the supervisory authority publishes such information and decides to rescind the direction, it must, without delay,
-- publish that fact in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A).
-- src:709 | (13B) Where the supervisory authority publishes such information and the supervisory authority decides to rescind the direction to which the notice relates, the supervisory authority must, without delay, publish that fact in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A).
@ref reg 25(13B) (src:709-709)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has published, without delay, the fact that the direction is rescinded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it published that fact in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has published information under paragraph (13A) and has decided to rescind the direction to which the notice relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(13B) the supervisory authority has published the rescission without delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the supervisory authority has published information under paragraph (13A) and has decided to rescind the direction to which the notice relates`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the supervisory authority has published information under paragraph (13A) and has decided to rescind the direction to which the notice relates" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the supervisory authority has published, without delay, the fact that the direction is rescinded` AND `it published that fact in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the supervisory authority must, without delay, publish that fact in the same manner" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(13C).  Where the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (13A) and the person to whom the notice is given refers the
-- matter to the Upper Tribunal, the authority must, without delay, publish information about the status of the appeal and its outcome in the same manner.
-- src:710 | (13C) Where the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (13A) and the person to whom the notice is given refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal, the supervisory authority must, without delay, publish information about the status of the appeal and its outcome in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A).
