GIVEN `the supervisory authority has published, without delay, information about the status of the appeal and its outcome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it published that information in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has published information under paragraph (13A) and the person to whom the notice is given has referred the matter to the Upper Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(13C) the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the supervisory authority has published information under paragraph (13A) and the person to whom the notice is given has referred the matter to the Upper Tribunal`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the supervisory authority has published information under paragraph (13A) and the person to whom the notice is given has referred the matter to the Upper Tribunal" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `the supervisory authority has published, without delay, information about the status of the appeal and its outcome` AND `it published that information in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (13A)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the supervisory authority must, without delay, publish information about the status of the appeal and its outcome" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 25(14)(a).  "Appropriate tribunal" means (i) the Upper Tribunal, in the case of a direction issued by the FCA; (ii) the First-tier or
-- Upper Tribunal, as provided for in regulation 99, in the case of a direction issued by the Commissioners.
DECLARE `reg 25(14) issuer of the direction` IS ONE OF
    `reg 25(14)(a)(i) the FCA`
    `reg 25(14)(a)(ii) the Commissioners`
    `reg 25(14) another supervisory authority`

DECLARE `reg 25(14) tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `reg 25(14)(a)(i) the Upper Tribunal`
    `reg 25(14)(a)(ii) the First-tier or Upper Tribunal, as provided for in regulation 99`
    `reg 25(14) no appropriate tribunal named`

-- src:711 | (14) For the purpose of this regulation—
-- src:712 | (a) “appropriate tribunal” means—
-- src:713 | (i) the Upper Tribunal, in the case of a direction issued by the FCA;
-- src:714 | (ii) the First-tier or Upper Tribunal, as provided for in regulation 99, in the case of a direction issued by the Commissioners;
-- src:715 | (b) “specified” means specified in the direction.
@ref reg 25(14) (src:711-715)
GIVEN issuer IS A `reg 25(14) issuer of the direction`
GIVETH A `reg 25(14) tribunal`
`reg 25(14)(a) the appropriate tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER issuer
    WHEN `reg 25(14)(a)(i) the FCA` THEN `reg 25(14)(a)(i) the Upper Tribunal`
    WHEN `reg 25(14)(a)(ii) the Commissioners` THEN `reg 25(14)(a)(ii) the First-tier or Upper Tribunal, as provided for in regulation 99`
    WHEN `reg 25(14) another supervisory authority` THEN `reg 25(14) no appropriate tribunal named` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (14)(a) names the tribunal for a direction issued by the FCA and by the Commissioners only

-- reg 25(14)(b).  "Specified" means specified in the direction.
@ref reg 25(14)(b) (src:715-715)
GIVEN `the person or description is specified in the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 25(14)(b) the person or description is specified` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person or description is specified in the direction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified” means specified in the direction"
